   "why": "Design 5 re-centred, with the rhythm retuned (the bounded push's first step; the owner: 'Agree, option 1'). E's resting output (~0.15) times its copy weight pushed F's and SL's input ~1 down, so SL sat near 0 in dim light and Dm saturated, and the cell ran 73-79% of the time there. F and SL bias -0.3 -> +0.75 puts F back mid-range (input + bias ~-0.2 in dim light, ~+0.15 bright). SL's span by light is now narrow (~0.46 at light 0.02 to ~0.54 bright: the wall's resting sum changes little at bias -3.7), so Dm = sigma(4 - 8 SL) spans only ~0.58 to ~0.42. Dm -> Q -6 -> -8 and Q bias 0.1 -> 1.7 then put R2's flip-on (Q_out 0.25, y_Q ~-2.8) just above Q's bright rest target (~-3.1) and well above its dim one (~-4.2): calculated with tau 250, bright runs ~43 ticks and rests ~395 (~10% running), dim runs ~52 and rests ~150 (~26%). The copy weight -6.5 -> -7.0, a small step toward cancelling bright runs (short by ~+3 in design 5); in the far field it now over-cancels slightly. Everything else is design 5's. Expected in probes: running ~20-30% in dim light, ~10% bright; bumps pulling 0.5-0.8; bright runs shorter than design 5's ~400 ticks. The rests in bright light hinge on Dm to within ~0.05, so the rhythm may land off its calculation."
